From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:51:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] presentation: lay panorama cells left to right unless a lane
 is recessed by half

The staggered grid always dropped the next cell into the shortest lane, so a
right lane only a few pixels shorter left a hole on the left. Changing the
column count (a foldable going from 2 to 4) also reflowed only the visible
items until the next scroll.

Panorama mode now measures a LazyLayout masonry. Every rectangle is computed
in one pass: a cell goes to the leftmost lane whose bottom is within half of
that cell's height of the shortest lane. Full-line rows (search bar, section
title, loading row) sit on the deepest lane and realign the others. Cover
heights come from the committed wide/tall band (3/2 or 2/3, plus the 4 dp
cell padding and, for comfortable grids, 4 dp plus two 18 sp title lines).
A column or width change records the viewport-top item and its offset and
restores that scroll in the same measure.

The fast scroller uses the known content height instead of the staggered
estimate. Library, browse, and related panorama grids call the new layout.
Regular grids are unchanged.

Homologous with mihon-harmony 0021. This patch is anikku-harmony 0030.
